# 🚨 CURSOR AGENT RULES - SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH

## MANDATORY FOR ALL CURSOR AGENTS

### 🔴 CRITICAL: Read Master Rules

**BEFORE ANY WORK:**
1. Read `.cursor/rules/MASTER-RULES-INDEX.mdc` (MASTER INDEX - SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH)
2. Check branch: `git branch --show-current`
3. Pull latest: `git pull origin <target-branch>` (typically `beta`)

### Quick Reference

**Complete rules are in**: `.cursor/rules/MASTER-RULES-INDEX.mdc` (master index with modular rule files)

**Key points**:
- ✅ **FULL AUTOMATION**: All git operations, validation, and fixes are automatic (see `CORE-AUTOMATION.mdc`)
- ✅ Feature branches with PRs (not direct beta commits)
- ✅ Bash validation on push (auto-fix errors, batched)
- ✅ Automated merge with conflict resolution
- ✅ Sequential PR merging (one at a time)
- ✅ Immediate feedback in chat (informational only)
- ✅ **Batching**: All fixes collected → Single commit → Single push (clean build tree)

### Modular Rule Structure

**8 focused modules (all under 500 lines):**
- `CORE-AUTOMATION.mdc` - Full automation principles (READ FIRST)
- `AGENT-BEHAVIOR.mdc` - File creation, response mode, core files
- `GIT-WORKFLOW.mdc` - Git operations, PR workflow, branch management
- `VALIDATION.mdc` - Validation triggers, bash validation, CoT checks
- `MERGE-CONFLICTS.mdc` - Merge and conflict resolution
- `CLOUD-AGENTS.mdc` - Cloud agent specifics
- `COMMUNICATION.mdc` - User communication and feedback
- `BEST-PRACTICES.mdc` - Best practices compliance

### When in Doubt

**STOP. READ MASTER-RULES-INDEX.mdc. ASK USER. WAIT FOR APPROVAL.**

---

**These rules are MANDATORY and STRICTLY ENFORCED.**
**Cursor IDE will monitor compliance.**
